# 8. User interface: market-data transparency and controls

Create a polished, responsive “Market Data & Connections” area consistent with the existing design system. Do not create a separate visual language.

## 8.1 Gold price card

The primary gold price card should show:
- Instrument name and type, e.g. `XAU/USD Spot Reference`.
- Price and currency/unit, e.g. `USD / troy oz`.
- Price type: bid, ask, midpoint, last, mark or reference.
- Provider name and data classification badge.
- Source timestamp and “received/updated” timestamp.
- Human-readable age, e.g. `Updated 4 seconds ago`.
- Connection/health state.
- Market session state if known.
- Change and percentage change only when the comparison basis is known.
- A clear stale, delayed, unavailable or simulated banner when applicable.

Avoid using green “LIVE” indicators unless live status is verified by provider metadata/capability and freshness checks. Use both text and visual status so meaning is not conveyed by colour alone.

## 8.2 Provider configuration screen

Include:
- Provider list/cards with enabled state, supported instrument types, current health and entitlement state.
- Primary source selector.
- Optional fallback selector with compatibility validation.
- Canonical instrument and provider-symbol mapping editor.
- Live/delayed/indicative/snapshot support labels.
- Refresh interval and freshness policy settings.
- “Test connection”, “Test quote”, “Refresh now” and “View diagnostics” actions.
- Last successful quote, last error, last transition and latency.
- Secure credential input with masked values.
- “Clear credential” and “rotate credential” actions where applicable.
- A warning when a selected provider cannot supply the requested instrument.
- A warning when live data requires a subscription, permission, or provider plan.

A successful API authentication must not automatically show “Live data connected”. Distinguish `Authenticated`, `Instrument supported`, `Market data permission verified`, `Receiving valid quote`, and `Quote fresh`.

## 8.3 Diagnostics panel

For an authorized user, provide a safe diagnostic view showing:
- Configured primary and fallback sources.
- Canonical instrument mapping.
- Provider status and recent latency.
- Latest source timestamp, receive timestamp and age.
- Last error category and redacted message.
- Retry/backoff/circuit-breaker status.
- Recent source switches and data-quality rejections.
- Whether a recommendation is currently blocked due to data quality.
- A copyable, sanitized diagnostic report.

Never expose API keys, bot tokens, passwords, authorization headers, session cookies, full account identifiers or other secrets in the UI, logs or exported diagnostics.

## 8.4 Responsive and accessible behaviour

Support desktop, tablet and mobile layouts. Make status text readable, controls keyboard accessible, labels explicit and error messages actionable. Avoid a dashboard full of decorative green dots that mask the actual data state.

