# 18. Definition of done / acceptance criteria

The work is not complete until the following are demonstrated:

### Market data
- [ ] The original incorrect-price defect has a documented, evidence-based root cause.
- [ ] The default configured source can retrieve a valid quote for the explicitly selected instrument using a permitted access method.
- [ ] The app does not confuse spot gold, futures, ETFs, CFDs or physical retail rates.
- [ ] The displayed quote includes price type, currency/unit, provider, source timestamp and age.
- [ ] Live/delayed/indicative/snapshot/cached/stale/unavailable states are represented accurately.
- [ ] A successful HTTP response alone cannot mark a quote live.
- [ ] Stale or invalid quotes cannot silently enter new recommendations.
- [ ] All downstream consumers use the canonical validated market-data service.
- [ ] Fallback never silently substitutes an incompatible instrument.
- [ ] Provider outage results in a clear unavailable/degraded state, not a fake price.

### Configuration and broker connections
- [ ] Provider configuration is editable and validated.
- [ ] Unsupported instrument mappings are clearly rejected.
- [ ] Optional broker adapters are disabled by default and are only enabled after capability and entitlement verification.
- [ ] Missing live-data entitlement is shown honestly.
- [ ] Secrets are stored and redacted safely.
- [ ] No orders or brokerage transactions are submitted.

### Notifications
- [ ] Telegram can be configured and tested end to end.
- [ ] Other enabled channels have real, tested adapters.
- [ ] App-status, data-quality, provider transition and advisory notifications can be enabled/disabled by category.
- [ ] Routing, severity, quiet hours, deduplication, rate limits and retries work as configured.
- [ ] Failed delivery is visible and does not break market-data processing.
- [ ] Recovery events are sent according to policy.
- [ ] No notification presents stale/unverified data as live.

### Quality and operations
- [ ] Unit, adapter contract, integration and regression tests pass.
- [ ] Existing features remain functional.
- [ ] No duplicate quote logic or duplicate notification pipeline has been introduced.
- [ ] Health/status screens and diagnostic logs agree with actual runtime state.
- [ ] Configuration, setup, troubleshooting, licensing caveats and known limitations are documented.
- [ ] The final report identifies changed files/modules, test commands and results, setup steps, remaining gaps and release recommendation.

A checklist item must not be marked complete merely because code exists. It requires a test, observable evidence or a documented reason why the item is not applicable.

